{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-28229-r4513507","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Frikadeller (Danish Meatballs)","sourcePageId":28229,"sourceRevision":"4513507","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:05:46Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Frikadeller%20(Danish%20Meatballs)&oldid=4513507","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Danish recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Pan fried recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground pork","Category:Recipes using veal","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"8f5fcc808ec098b8588e57fef28d0cef1093ffa7e430e5e73b7e736f73f7449a","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Frikadeller.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Denmark|Danish Cuisine]]\n\n'''Frikadeller''' are as [[w:Denmark|Danish]] as the [[w:Dannebrog|Dannebrog]]. This is standard Danish fare, made of ground [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] and [[Cookbook:Veal|veal]] and traditionally served with [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiled]] [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], [[Cookbook:Gravy|gravy]] and [[Cookbook:Rødkål|rødkål]] ([[Cookbook:Braising|braised]] red [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]]). Originally, this dish was made so that the meat would feed more people, and thus, the possibilities as to what can be added are numerous.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*250 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] (about 0.5 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]]) ground [[Cookbook:Veal|veal]]\n*250 grams ground [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]]\n*1 large [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*20% by volume (about ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]]) of [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|bread crumbs]]\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Mince|Minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] (optional)\n*Ground [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]] to taste\n*Butter\n\n==Procedure==\n#Mix all ingredients except butter together.\n#Shape mixture into small patties.\n#[[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] in hot [[Cookbook:Skillet|skillet]] with lots of butter.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* These can be frozen and reheated.\n* You can substitute bread crumbs with [[Cookbook:Wheat Germ|wheat germ]] and/or [[Cookbook:Oat Bran|oat bran]].\n* Any ingredient will work. Many people add a quantity of [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]] also, and the mixture is then thickened again with more flour, bread crumbs and/or oat bran.\n\n[[Category:Danish recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using veal|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground pork|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Frikadeller (Danish Meatballs)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"ser